"021:001 And the Lord visited Sarrha, as he said, and the Lord did to Sarrha, as he spoke.",
"021:002 And she conceived and bore to Abraam a son in old age, at the set time according as the Lord spoke to him.",
"021:003 And Abraam called the name of his son that was born to him, whom Sarrha bore to him, Isaac.",
"021:004 And Abraam circumcised Isaac on the eighth day, as God commanded him.",
"021:005 And Abraam was one hundred years old when Isaac his son was born to him.",
"021:006 And Sarrha said, The Lord has made laughter for me, for whoever shall hear shall rejoice with me.",
"021:007 And she said, Who shall say to Abraam that Sarrha suckles a child? for I have born a child in my old age.",
"021:008 And the child grew and was weaned, and Abraam made a great feast the day that his son Isaac was weaned.",
"021:009 And Sarrha having seen the son of Agar the Egyptian who was born to Abraam, sporting with Isaac her son,",
"021:010 then she said to Abraam, Cast out this bondwoman and her son, for the son of this bondwoman shall not inherit with my son Isaac.",
"021:011 But the word appeared very hard before Abraam concerning his son.",
"021:012 But God said to Abraam, Let it not be hard before you concerning the child, and concerning the bondwoman; in all things whatever Sarrha shall say to you, hear her voice, for in Isaac shall your seed be called.",
"021:013 And moreover I will make the son of this bondwoman a great nation, because he is your seed.",
"021:014 And Abraam rose up in the morning and took loaves and a skin of water, and gave them to Agar, and he put the child on her shoulder, and sent her away, and she having departed wandered in the wilderness near the well of the oath.",
"021:015 And the water failed out of the skin, and she cast the child under a fir tree.",
"021:016 And she departed and sat down opposite him at a distance, as it were a bow-shot, for she said, Surely I can’t see the death of my child: and she sat opposite him, and the child cried aloud and wept.",
"021:017 And God heard the voice of the child from the place where he was, and an angel of God called Agar out of heaven, and said to her, What is it, Agar? fear not, for God has heard the voice of the child from the place where he is.",
"021:018 Rise up, and take the child, and hold him in your hand, for I will make him a great nation.",
"021:019 And God opened her eyes, and she saw a well of springing water; and she went and filled the skin with water, and gave the child drink.",
"021:020 And God was with the child, and he grew and lived in the wilderness, and became an archer.",
"021:021 And he lived in the wilderness, and his mother took him a wife out of Pharan of Egypt.",
"021:022 And it came to pass at that time that Abimelech spoke, and Ochozath his friend, and Phichol the chief captain of his host, to Abraam, saying, God is with you in all things, whatever you may do.",
"021:023 Now therefore swear to me by God that you will not injure me, nor my seed, nor my name, but according to the righteousness which I have performed with you you shall deal with me, and with the land in which you have sojourned.",
"021:024 And Abraam said, I will swear.",
"021:025 And Abraam reproved Abimelech because of the wells of water, which the servants of Abimelech took away.",
"021:026 And Abimelech said to him, I know not who has done this thing to you, neither did you tell it me, neither heard I it but only today.",
"021:027 And Abraam took sheep and calves, and gave them to Abimelech, and both made a covenant.",
"021:028 And Abraam set seven ewe-lambs by themselves.",
"021:029 And Abimelech said to Abraam, What are these seven ewe-lambs which you have set alone?",
"021:030 And Abraam said, You shall receive the seven ewe-lambs of me, that they may be for me as a witness, that I dug this well.",
"021:031 Therefore he named the name of that place, The Well of the Oath, for there they both swore.",
"021:032 And they made a covenant at the well of the oath. And there rose up Abimelech, Ochozath his friend, and Phichol the commander-in-chief of his army, and they returned to the land of the Phylistines.",
"021:033 And Abraam planted a field at the well of the oath, and called there on the name of the Lord, the everlasting God.",
"021:034 And Abraam sojourned in the land of the Phylistines many days."
