"023:001 And the life of Sarrha was one hundred and twenty-seven years.",
"023:002 And Sarrha died in the city of Arboc, which is in the valley, this is Chebron in the land of Chanaan; and Abraam came to lament for Sarrha and to mourn.",
"023:003 And Abraam stood up from before his dead; and Abraam spoke to the sons of Chet, saying,",
"023:004 I am a sojourner and a stranger amongst you, give me therefore possession of a burying-place amongst you, and I will bury my dead away from me.",
"023:005 And the sons of Chet answered to Abraam, saying, Not so, Sir,",
"023:006 but hear us; you are in the midst of us a king from God; bury your dead in our choice sepulchres, for not one of us will by any means withhold his sepulchre from you, so that you should not bury your dead there.",
"023:007 And Abraam rose up and did obeisance to the people of the land, to the sons of Chet.",
"023:008 And Abraam spoke to them, saying, If you have it in your mind that I should bury my dead out of my sight, listen to me, and speak for me to Ephron the son Saar.",
"023:009 And let him give me the double cave which he has, which is in a part of his field, let him give it me for the money it is worth for possession of a burying-place amongst you.",
"023:010 Now Ephron was sitting in the midst of the children of Chet, and Ephron the Chettite answered Abraam and spoke in the hearing of the sons of Chet, and of all who entered the city, saying,",
"023:011 Attend to me, my lord, and hear me, I give to you the field and the cave which is in it; I have given it you before all my country men; bury your dead.",
"023:012 And Abraam did obeisance before the people of the land.",
"023:013 And he said in the ears of Ephron before the people of the land, Since you are on my side, hear me; take the price of the field from me, and I will bury my dead there.",
"023:014 But Ephron answered Abraam, saying,",
"023:015 Nay, my lord, I have heard indeed, the land is worth four hundred silver didrachmas, but what can this be between me and you? nay, do you bury your dead.",
"023:016 And Abraam listened to Ephron, and Abraam rendered to Ephron the money, which he mentioned in the ears of the sons of Chet, four hundred didrachmas of silver approved with merchants.",
"023:017 And the field of Ephron, which was in Double Cave, which is opposite Mambre, the field and the cave, which was in it, and every tree which was in the field, and whatever is in its borders round about, were made sure in its borders round about, were made sure",
"023:018 to Abraam for a possession, before the sons of Chet, and all that entered into the city.",
"023:019 After this Abraam buried Sarrha his wife in the Double Cave of the field, which is opposite Mambre, this is Chebron in the land of Chanaan.",
"023:020 So the field and the cave which was in it were made sure to Abraam for possession of a burying place, by the sons of Chet."
