"040:001 And it came to pass after these things, that the chief cupbearer of the king of Egypt and the chief baker trespassed against their lord the king of Egypt.",
"040:002 And Pharao was angry with his two eunuchs, with his chief cupbearer, and with his chief baker.",
"040:003 And he put them in ward, into the prison, into the place whereinto Joseph had been led.",
"040:004 And the chief keeper of the prison committed them to Joseph, and he stood by them; and they were some days in the prison.",
"040:005 And they both had a dream in one night; and the vision of the dream of the chief cupbearer and chief baker, who belonged to the king of Egypt, who were in the prison, was this.",
"040:006 Joseph went in to them in the morning, and saw them, and they had been troubled.",
"040:007 And he asked the eunuchs of Pharao who were with him in the prison with his master, saying, Why is it that your countenances are sad today?",
"040:008 And they said to him, We have seen a dream, and there is no interpreter of it. And Joseph said to them, Is not the interpretation of them through god? tell them than to me.",
"040:009 And the chief cupbearer related his dream to Joseph, and said, In my dream a vine was before me.",
"040:010 And in the vine were three stems; and it budding shot forth blossoms; the clusters of grapes were ripe.",
"040:011 And the cup of Pharao was in my hand; and I took the bunch of grapes, and squeezed it into the cup, and gave the cup into Pharao's hand.",
"040:012 And Joseph said to him, This is the interpretation of it. The three stems are three days.",
"040:013 Yet three days and Pharao shall remember your office, and he shall restore you to your place of chief cupbearer, and you shall give the cup of Pharao into his hand, according to your former high place, as you were wont to be cupbearer.",
"040:014 But remember me of yourself, when it shall be well with you, and you shall deal mercifully with me, and you shall make mention of me to Pharao, and you shall bring me forth out of this dungeon.",
"040:015 For surely I was stolen away out of the land of the Hebrews, and here I have done nothing, but they have cast me into this pit.",
"040:016 And the chief baker saw that he interpreted aright; and he said to Joseph, I also saw a dream, and I thought I took up on my head three baskets of mealy food.",
"040:017 And in the upper basket there was the work of the baker of every kind which Pharao eats; and the fowls of the air ate them out of the basket that was on my head.",
"040:018 And Joseph answered and said to him, This is the interpretation of it; The three baskets are three days.",
"040:019 Yet three days, and Pharao shall take away your head from off you, and shall hang you on a tree, and the birds of the sky shall eat your flesh from off you.",
"040:020 And it came to pass on the third day that it was Pharao's birth-day, and he made a banquet for all his servants, and he remembered the office of the cupbearer and the office of the baker in the midst of his servants.",
"040:021 And he restored the chief cupbearer to his office, and he gave the cup into Pharao's hand.",
"040:022 And he hanged the chief baker, as Joseph, interpreted to them.",
"040:023 Yet did not the chief cupbearer remember Joseph, but forgot him."
